// expect: 16
// A NESTED FN WITH A DEFAULT CANNOT BE CALLED. `g(1)` is g(1, 5) = 6, plus
// `k`. The emit writes `(unreachable) ;; partial over non-global callee
// shape` at the call and the program traps (measured 2026-09-25) with a
// clean check: the omitted field is filled by looking the callee up by NAME
// at lowering, and a nested fn is no longer in the environment by then.
//
// Retires when a default is lowered once, in its callee's scope
// (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge).
fn outer(k) = {
  fn g(a, b = 5) = a + b
  g(1) + k
}

fn main() = outer(10)
